<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept importance="optional" id="t00569">
	<title>Safe Exit Warning (SEW)</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>safe exit warning (SEW)</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig>
								<figgroup>
									<image align="center" href="../../images/M_CT27_D10_005_E.eps" scale="95" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<p>While your vehicle is stopped, and if Safe Exit Warning detects a vehicle approaching the rear corner of your vehicle and a passenger opens a door, Safe Exit Warning may warn you with a warning message and a warning sound to help avoid a collision.</p>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<note type="caution">
			<p>Warning timing may vary depending on the speed of the approaching vehicle.</p>
		</note>
		<section>
			<title>Detecting sensor</title>
			<note type="caution">
				<p>For more details on the precautions of the rear corner radars, refer to <xref type="concept" href="t00558.dita#t00558">Blind-Spot Collision-Avoidance Assist (BCA)</xref>.</p>
			</note>
		</section>
	</conbody>
</concept>